From 92f8cd05e790d903e37ba4309e1f633042aa7fcd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 2 Jun 2026 17:58:02 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] dos: patch 0087 -- device-rate experiment lever (v1.0.8
 organya-delivery)

The SB16 PCM device opens at 44100 Hz stereo because SDL core floors every
physical playback device to max(DEFAULT_AUDIO_PLAYBACK_FREQUENCY=44100,
requested) (SDL_audio.c PrepareAudioFormat), not because the hardware needs
it. The engine's Tier-2 11025-mono MIX request only configures the logical
device; SDL inserts a logical->physical resampler (11025 mono -> 44100 stereo,
4x upsample + mono->stereo dup) and the DSP is programmed at 44100. Net: the
DMA ring drains 4x faster than the content needs AND a 4x resampler runs every
pump -- the audio-delivery bottleneck behind organya's slow tempo on the
DX2-66 (the synth has ~5.65x headroom; it is delivery-bound, not synth-bound).

SDL explicitly licenses the backend to change spec.freq in OpenDevice and
re-honors it via a second SDL_UpdatedAudioDeviceFormat. This lever overrides
device->spec.freq to an operator-requested rate via SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_DEVICE_RATE
(strict integer, clamped to the SB16 [5000,44100] range). DEFAULT UNSET = no
change = byte-identical to pre-0087 (the 44100 floor stands; zero production
risk; OPL3/WaveBlaster are out-of-band MIDI and never touch this PCM path).
Self-verifying via the existing SDL/0073 rate-diag (req_freq vs dev_freq
divergence) + rate-meas (hw_frame_rate) + SDL/0074 RATEDIV-auto lines.

Experiment lever for the v1.0.8 device-rate sweep; ship-form setter
(SDL_DOSAudioSetDeviceFrameRate) + ring-fill query are follow-ons.
---
 src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c | 68 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 68 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
index 53a828396..cde248f53 100644
--- a/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
+++ b/src/audio/dos/SDL_dosaudio_sb.c
@@ -2097,6 +2097,74 @@ static bool DOSSOUNDBLASTER_OpenDevice(SDL_AudioDevice *device)
     if (!is_sb16 && device->spec.freq > 22050) {
         device->spec.freq = 22050; // clamp to safe max for pre-SB16
     }
+
+    /* DOSKUTSU patch (patch 0087): device-rate experiment lever.
+       v1.0.8 organya-delivery campaign. flush-instr's calib read + nx-engine's
+       DAC-vs-content trace found the SB16 PCM device runs at 44100 Hz while the
+       synth/mixer content is Tier-2 11025 mono. The 44100 is NOT a hardware
+       requirement: SDL core FLOORS every physical playback device to
+       max(DEFAULT_AUDIO_PLAYBACK_FREQUENCY=44100, requested) at
+       SDL_audio.c:~1851 (a quality-floor policy), so the engine's 11025-mono
+       MIX_CreateMixerDevice request only configures the LOGICAL device and SDL
+       inserts a logical->physical SDL_AudioStream that resamples 11025 mono ->
+       44100 stereo (a 4x upsample + mono->stereo dup) on the pull path. The DSP
+       is then programmed at device->spec.freq = 44100 (sb.c 0x41 write below).
+       Net: the DMA ring drains 4x faster than the content needs AND a 4x
+       resampler runs every pump -- the audio-DELIVERY bottleneck behind the
+       organya slow tempo (synth itself has ~5.65x headroom -- delivery-bound,
+       not synth-bound).
+
+       SDL_audio.c:~1843 explicitly licenses the backend to change spec.freq in
+       OpenDevice ("These are just requests! The backend may change any of these
+       values during OpenDevice method!") and re-honors it via a second
+       SDL_UpdatedAudioDeviceFormat after impl.OpenDevice returns. The SB16
+       supports 5000..44100 Hz via DSP cmd 0x41 (see the comment above). So this
+       lever overrides device->spec.freq to the operator-requested rate; opening
+       at 11025 (== content) cuts the ring drain 4x, collapses the resampler to a
+       cheap channel-dup, and auto-collapses the Bug 6 RATEDIV to identity (the
+       dos_pixtone_recompute_ratediv reads the new dev_freq below).
+
+       Env-gated, DEFAULT UNSET = no change = byte-identical to pre-0087 (the
+       44100 floor stands; zero production risk; OPL3 / WaveBlaster are
+       out-of-band MIDI and never touch this PCM path). Strict integer parse,
+       clamped to the SB16 HW range [5000, 44100]; out-of-range is ignored (no
+       change) with a diagnostic.
+
+       SELF-VERIFYING: placed AFTER the rate-diag req-snapshot (dos_rd_req_freq
+       above) so the SDL/0073 rate-diag line shows req_freq=<SDL floor> vs
+       dev_freq=<override> -- "they differ" == the override took, settling the
+       v1.0.1 "device rate not controllable SDL-side" question on the first
+       cell. The SDL/0073 rate-meas hw_frame_rate then confirms the DAC actually
+       reprogrammed (drops to ~the override), and SDL/0074 RATEDIV-auto confirms
+       the divider tracked. No new instrumentation needed.
+
+       SHIP-FORM follow-on (NOT in this experiment patch): a setter
+       SDL_DOSAudioSetDeviceFrameRate(SAMPLE_RATE) called from SoundManager so
+       production auto-derives the rate without an env var (default-ON +
+       killswitch). Hint wins over the setter when both are present. */
+    {
+        const char *dr_hint = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_DEVICE_RATE");
+        if (dr_hint && dr_hint[0] != '\0') {
+            const int dr = SDL_atoi(dr_hint);
+            if (dr >= 5000 && dr <= 44100) {
+                const int dr_prev = device->spec.freq;
+                device->spec.freq = dr;
+                doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0087 device-rate override: %d -> %d Hz "
+                                 "(SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_DOS_AUDIO_DEVICE_RATE; SB16 DSP "
+                                 "0x41 will program %d; logical->physical resample "
+                                 "collapses toward content rate; Bug6 RATEDIV "
+                                 "auto-recomputes from the new dev_freq)",
+                                 dr_prev, dr, dr);
+            } else {
+                doskutsu_dbg_log("audio: SDL/0087 device-rate override IGNORED: "
+                                 "%d Hz out of SB16 range [5000,44100] -- staying "
+                                 "at %d Hz", dr, device->spec.freq);
+            }
+        }
+        /* default (hint unset): no change. device->spec.freq stays the SDL-floored
+           value (44100) -- byte-identical to pre-0087. */
+    }
+
     device->sample_frames = SDL_GetDefaultSampleFramesFromFreq(device->spec.freq);
 
     // Calculate the final parameters for this audio specification
-- 
